    "section": "Task 3: List Practice",
    "text": "Task 3: List Practice\n\nCreate a new data frame with new data that is similar to the previous data frame.\n\n\n# create a similar data frame to the first one (Task 2)\n# repeating steps from Task 1 and 2\n\n# create two new vectors of pre-measurements and post-measurements of the second experiment \npre_bp2 &lt;- c(138, 135, 147, 117, 152, 134, 114, 121, 131, 130)\npost_bp2 &lt;- c(105, 136, 123, 130, 134, 143, 135, 139, 120, 124)\n\n# create pre_bp2 and post_bp2 objects\nnames(pre_bp2) &lt;- paste(\"Subject\", 1:10, sep = \"_\")\nnames(post_bp2) &lt;- paste(\"Subject\", 1:10, sep = \"_\")\n\npre_bp2\n\n Subject_1  Subject_2  Subject_3  Subject_4  Subject_5  Subject_6  Subject_7 \n       138        135        147        117        152        134        114 \n Subject_8  Subject_9 Subject_10 \n       121        131        130 \n\npost_bp2\n\n Subject_1  Subject_2  Subject_3  Subject_4  Subject_5  Subject_6  Subject_7 \n       105        136        123        130        134        143        135 \n Subject_8  Subject_9 Subject_10 \n       139        120        124 \n\n# create diff_bp2 object\ndiff_bp2 &lt;- pre_bp2 - post_bp2\ndiff_bp2\n\n Subject_1  Subject_2  Subject_3  Subject_4  Subject_5  Subject_6  Subject_7 \n        33         -1         24        -13         18         -9        -21 \n Subject_8  Subject_9 Subject_10 \n       -18         11          6 \n\n# create post_less_120_2 object\npost_less_120_2 &lt;- post_bp2 &lt; 120\npost_less_120_2\n\n Subject_1  Subject_2  Subject_3  Subject_4  Subject_5  Subject_6  Subject_7 \n      TRUE      FALSE      FALSE      FALSE      FALSE      FALSE      FALSE \n Subject_8  Subject_9 Subject_10 \n     FALSE      FALSE      FALSE \n\n# create patients2 object\npatients2 &lt;- names(pre_bp2)\npatients2\n\n [1] \"Subject_1\"  \"Subject_2\"  \"Subject_3\"  \"Subject_4\"  \"Subject_5\" \n [6] \"Subject_6\"  \"Subject_7\"  \"Subject_8\"  \"Subject_9\"  \"Subject_10\"\n\n# create second data frame that is similar to the previous\nbp_df2 &lt;- data.frame(\n  patients = patients2,\n  pre_bp = pre_bp2,\n  post_bp = post_bp2,\n  diff_bp = diff_bp2,\n  post_under_120 = post_less_120_2\n)\nbp_df2\n\n             patients pre_bp post_bp diff_bp post_under_120\nSubject_1   Subject_1    138     105      33           TRUE\nSubject_2   Subject_2    135     136      -1          FALSE\nSubject_3   Subject_3    147     123      24          FALSE\nSubject_4   Subject_4    117     130     -13          FALSE\nSubject_5   Subject_5    152     134      18          FALSE\nSubject_6   Subject_6    134     143      -9          FALSE\nSubject_7   Subject_7    114     135     -21          FALSE\nSubject_8   Subject_8    121     139     -18          FALSE\nSubject_9   Subject_9    131     120      11          FALSE\nSubject_10 Subject_10    130     124       6          FALSE\n\n# print data frame nicely\nknitr::kable(bp_df2)\n\nWarning in attr(x, \"align\"): 'xfun::attr()' is deprecated.\nUse 'xfun::attr2()' instead.\nSee help(\"Deprecated\")\n\n\nWarning in attr(x, \"format\"): 'xfun::attr()' is deprecated.\nUse 'xfun::attr2()' instead.\nSee help(\"Deprecated\")\n\n\n\n\n\n\npatients\npre_bp\npost_bp\ndiff_bp\npost_under_120\n\n\n\n\nSubject_1\nSubject_1\n138\n105\n33\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_2\nSubject_2\n135\n136\n-1\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_3\nSubject_3\n147\n123\n24\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_4\nSubject_4\n117\n130\n-13\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_5\nSubject_5\n152\n134\n18\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_6\nSubject_6\n134\n143\n-9\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_7\nSubject_7\n114\n135\n-21\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_8\nSubject_8\n121\n139\n-18\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_9\nSubject_9\n131\n120\n11\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_10\nSubject_10\n130\n124\n6\nFALSE\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCreate and store a list with two elements:\n\n\n1st element named treatment and contains the first data frame\n2nd element named placebo and contains the second data frame\n\n\n# create treatment and placebo objects for each corresponding dataframe\ntreatment &lt;- bp_df1\nplacebo &lt;- bp_df2\n\n# create list with treatment and placebo using list()\nbp_exp &lt;- list(treatment = treatment, placebo = placebo)\nbp_exp\n\n$treatment\n            patients1 pre_bp1 post_bp1 diff_bp1 post_less_120_1\nSubject_1   Subject_1     130      114       16            TRUE\nSubject_2   Subject_2     128       98       30            TRUE\nSubject_3   Subject_3     116      113        3            TRUE\nSubject_4   Subject_4     124       99       25            TRUE\nSubject_5   Subject_5     133      107       26            TRUE\nSubject_6   Subject_6     134      116       18            TRUE\nSubject_7   Subject_7     118      113        5            TRUE\nSubject_8   Subject_8     126      111       15            TRUE\nSubject_9   Subject_9     114      119       -5            TRUE\nSubject_10 Subject_10     127      117       10            TRUE\nSubject_11 Subject_11     141      101       40            TRUE\nSubject_12 Subject_12     138      119       19            TRUE\nSubject_13 Subject_13     128      130       -2           FALSE\nSubject_14 Subject_14     140      122       18           FALSE\nSubject_15 Subject_15     137      106       31            TRUE\nSubject_16 Subject_16     131      106       25            TRUE\nSubject_17 Subject_17     120      124       -4           FALSE\nSubject_18 Subject_18     128      102       26            TRUE\nSubject_19 Subject_19     139      117       22            TRUE\nSubject_20 Subject_20     135      113       22            TRUE\n\n$placebo\n             patients pre_bp post_bp diff_bp post_under_120\nSubject_1   Subject_1    138     105      33           TRUE\nSubject_2   Subject_2    135     136      -1          FALSE\nSubject_3   Subject_3    147     123      24          FALSE\nSubject_4   Subject_4    117     130     -13          FALSE\nSubject_5   Subject_5    152     134      18          FALSE\nSubject_6   Subject_6    134     143      -9          FALSE\nSubject_7   Subject_7    114     135     -21          FALSE\nSubject_8   Subject_8    121     139     -18          FALSE\nSubject_9   Subject_9    131     120      11          FALSE\nSubject_10 Subject_10    130     124       6          FALSE\n\n\n\nAccess the first list element using three different types of syntax.\n\n\n# first access using brackets [], returns a list containing the named element\nbp_exp[1]\n\n$treatment\n            patients1 pre_bp1 post_bp1 diff_bp1 post_less_120_1\nSubject_1   Subject_1     130      114       16            TRUE\nSubject_2   Subject_2     128       98       30            TRUE\nSubject_3   Subject_3     116      113        3            TRUE\nSubject_4   Subject_4     124       99       25            TRUE\nSubject_5   Subject_5     133      107       26            TRUE\nSubject_6   Subject_6     134      116       18            TRUE\nSubject_7   Subject_7     118      113        5            TRUE\nSubject_8   Subject_8     126      111       15            TRUE\nSubject_9   Subject_9     114      119       -5            TRUE\nSubject_10 Subject_10     127      117       10            TRUE\nSubject_11 Subject_11     141      101       40            TRUE\nSubject_12 Subject_12     138      119       19            TRUE\nSubject_13 Subject_13     128      130       -2           FALSE\nSubject_14 Subject_14     140      122       18           FALSE\nSubject_15 Subject_15     137      106       31            TRUE\nSubject_16 Subject_16     131      106       25            TRUE\nSubject_17 Subject_17     120      124       -4           FALSE\nSubject_18 Subject_18     128      102       26            TRUE\nSubject_19 Subject_19     139      117       22            TRUE\nSubject_20 Subject_20     135      113       22            TRUE\n\n# second access using double brackets [[]], returns the actual data frame \nbp_exp[[1]]\n\n            patients1 pre_bp1 post_bp1 diff_bp1 post_less_120_1\nSubject_1   Subject_1     130      114       16            TRUE\nSubject_2   Subject_2     128       98       30            TRUE\nSubject_3   Subject_3     116      113        3            TRUE\nSubject_4   Subject_4     124       99       25            TRUE\nSubject_5   Subject_5     133      107       26            TRUE\nSubject_6   Subject_6     134      116       18            TRUE\nSubject_7   Subject_7     118      113        5            TRUE\nSubject_8   Subject_8     126      111       15            TRUE\nSubject_9   Subject_9     114      119       -5            TRUE\nSubject_10 Subject_10     127      117       10            TRUE\nSubject_11 Subject_11     141      101       40            TRUE\nSubject_12 Subject_12     138      119       19            TRUE\nSubject_13 Subject_13     128      130       -2           FALSE\nSubject_14 Subject_14     140      122       18           FALSE\nSubject_15 Subject_15     137      106       31            TRUE\nSubject_16 Subject_16     131      106       25            TRUE\nSubject_17 Subject_17     120      124       -4           FALSE\nSubject_18 Subject_18     128      102       26            TRUE\nSubject_19 Subject_19     139      117       22            TRUE\nSubject_20 Subject_20     135      113       22            TRUE\n\n# third access using $, also returns just the data frame itself\nbp_exp$treatment\n\n            patients1 pre_bp1 post_bp1 diff_bp1 post_less_120_1\nSubject_1   Subject_1     130      114       16            TRUE\nSubject_2   Subject_2     128       98       30            TRUE\nSubject_3   Subject_3     116      113        3            TRUE\nSubject_4   Subject_4     124       99       25            TRUE\nSubject_5   Subject_5     133      107       26            TRUE\nSubject_6   Subject_6     134      116       18            TRUE\nSubject_7   Subject_7     118      113        5            TRUE\nSubject_8   Subject_8     126      111       15            TRUE\nSubject_9   Subject_9     114      119       -5            TRUE\nSubject_10 Subject_10     127      117       10            TRUE\nSubject_11 Subject_11     141      101       40            TRUE\nSubject_12 Subject_12     138      119       19            TRUE\nSubject_13 Subject_13     128      130       -2           FALSE\nSubject_14 Subject_14     140      122       18           FALSE\nSubject_15 Subject_15     137      106       31            TRUE\nSubject_16 Subject_16     131      106       25            TRUE\nSubject_17 Subject_17     120      124       -4           FALSE\nSubject_18 Subject_18     128      102       26            TRUE\nSubject_19 Subject_19     139      117       22            TRUE\nSubject_20 Subject_20     135      113       22            TRUE\n\n\n\nIn one line, access the placebo data frame, pre_bp2 column.\n\n\n# use [] and [[]] to access the pre_bp2 column as a data frame\nbp_exp[[2]] [2:2]\n\n           pre_bp\nSubject_1     138\nSubject_2     135\nSubject_3     147\nSubject_4     117\nSubject_5     152\nSubject_6     134\nSubject_7     114\nSubject_8     121\nSubject_9     131\nSubject_10    130\n\n# or use $ and [] to do the same \nbp_exp$placebo[2]\n\n           pre_bp\nSubject_1     138\nSubject_2     135\nSubject_3     147\nSubject_4     117\nSubject_5     152\nSubject_6     134\nSubject_7     114\nSubject_8     121\nSubject_9     131\nSubject_10    130\n\n# or use just $ to return the vector only\nbp_exp$placebo$pre_bp\n\n [1] 138 135 147 117 152 134 114 121 131 130"
