    "section": "",
    "text": "#Task 1: Basic Vector Practice\n\nCreate two vectors of the pre- and post-measurements:\n\n\npre_bp &lt;- c(130, 128, 116, 124, 133, 134, 118, 126, 114, 127, 141, 138, 128, 140, 137, 131, 120, 128, 139, 135)\n\npost_bp &lt;- c(114, 98, 113, 99, 107, 116, 113, 111, 119, 117, 101, 119, 130, 122, 106, 106, 124, 102, 117, 113)\n\n\nAssign names to the vector elements:\n\n\nnames(pre_bp)  &lt;- paste(\"Subject\", 1:20, sep = \"_\")\nnames(post_bp) &lt;- paste(\"Subject\", 1:20, sep = \"_\")\n\n\nCalculate the change (decrease?) in blood pressure accross all patients:\n\n\ndiff_bp &lt;- pre_bp - post_bp\ndiff_bp\n\n Subject_1  Subject_2  Subject_3  Subject_4  Subject_5  Subject_6  Subject_7 \n        16         30          3         25         26         18          5 \n Subject_8  Subject_9 Subject_10 Subject_11 Subject_12 Subject_13 Subject_14 \n        15         -5         10         40         19         -2         18 \nSubject_15 Subject_16 Subject_17 Subject_18 Subject_19 Subject_20 \n        31         25         -4         26         22         22 \n\n\n\nFind the average decrease in BP across all patients:\n\n\nmean(diff_bp)\n\n[1] 17\n\n\n\nPatients who experienced a deceased in BP after treatment:\n\n\nimproved_bp &lt;- which(diff_bp &gt; 0, useNames = TRUE)\n\n\nCreate a new vector object with only improvers and their BPs:\n\n\nimprovers &lt;- diff_bp[improved_bp]\n\n\nFind the mean of the improvers BPs:\n\n\nmean(improvers)\n\n[1] 20.64706\n\n\n#Task 2: Basic Data Frame Practice\n\nCreate a frame object with four columns using the 4 vectors from Task 1:\n\n\npatient_name &lt;- names(pre_bp)\nbp_df &lt;- data.frame(patient_name, pre_bp, post_bp, diff_bp )\n#Meh, I don't love the double naming here. Thoughts?\nbp_df\n\n           patient_name pre_bp post_bp diff_bp\nSubject_1     Subject_1    130     114      16\nSubject_2     Subject_2    128      98      30\nSubject_3     Subject_3    116     113       3\nSubject_4     Subject_4    124      99      25\nSubject_5     Subject_5    133     107      26\nSubject_6     Subject_6    134     116      18\nSubject_7     Subject_7    118     113       5\nSubject_8     Subject_8    126     111      15\nSubject_9     Subject_9    114     119      -5\nSubject_10   Subject_10    127     117      10\nSubject_11   Subject_11    141     101      40\nSubject_12   Subject_12    138     119      19\nSubject_13   Subject_13    128     130      -2\nSubject_14   Subject_14    140     122      18\nSubject_15   Subject_15    137     106      31\nSubject_16   Subject_16    131     106      25\nSubject_17   Subject_17    120     124      -4\nSubject_18   Subject_18    128     102      26\nSubject_19   Subject_19    139     117      22\nSubject_20   Subject_20    135     113      22\n\n\n\nReturn only rows with negative BP:\n\n\nsubset(bp_df, diff_bp &lt; 0)\n\n           patient_name pre_bp post_bp diff_bp\nSubject_9     Subject_9    114     119      -5\nSubject_13   Subject_13    128     130      -2\nSubject_17   Subject_17    120     124      -4\n\n\n\nAdd new col to df with TRUE if the post_bp is below 120.\n\n\nbp_df$low_bp &lt;- ifelse(bp_df$post_bp &lt; 120, TRUE, \"\") #Should we list BPs &gt;= 119 as FALSE?\nbp_df\n\n           patient_name pre_bp post_bp diff_bp low_bp\nSubject_1     Subject_1    130     114      16   TRUE\nSubject_2     Subject_2    128      98      30   TRUE\nSubject_3     Subject_3    116     113       3   TRUE\nSubject_4     Subject_4    124      99      25   TRUE\nSubject_5     Subject_5    133     107      26   TRUE\nSubject_6     Subject_6    134     116      18   TRUE\nSubject_7     Subject_7    118     113       5   TRUE\nSubject_8     Subject_8    126     111      15   TRUE\nSubject_9     Subject_9    114     119      -5   TRUE\nSubject_10   Subject_10    127     117      10   TRUE\nSubject_11   Subject_11    141     101      40   TRUE\nSubject_12   Subject_12    138     119      19   TRUE\nSubject_13   Subject_13    128     130      -2       \nSubject_14   Subject_14    140     122      18       \nSubject_15   Subject_15    137     106      31   TRUE\nSubject_16   Subject_16    131     106      25   TRUE\nSubject_17   Subject_17    120     124      -4       \nSubject_18   Subject_18    128     102      26   TRUE\nSubject_19   Subject_19    139     117      22   TRUE\nSubject_20   Subject_20    135     113      22   TRUE\n\n\n\nPrint the whole data frame.\n\n\nknitr::kable(bp_df)\n\nWarning in attr(x, \"align\"): 'xfun::attr()' is deprecated.\nUse 'xfun::attr2()' instead.\nSee help(\"Deprecated\")\n\n\nWarning in attr(x, \"format\"): 'xfun::attr()' is deprecated.\nUse 'xfun::attr2()' instead.\nSee help(\"Deprecated\")\n\n\n\n\n\n\npatient_name\npre_bp\npost_bp\ndiff_bp\nlow_bp\n\n\n\n\nSubject_1\nSubject_1\n130\n114\n16\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_2\nSubject_2\n128\n98\n30\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_3\nSubject_3\n116\n113\n3\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_4\nSubject_4\n124\n99\n25\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_5\nSubject_5\n133\n107\n26\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_6\nSubject_6\n134\n116\n18\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_7\nSubject_7\n118\n113\n5\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_8\nSubject_8\n126\n111\n15\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_9\nSubject_9\n114\n119\n-5\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_10\nSubject_10\n127\n117\n10\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_11\nSubject_11\n141\n101\n40\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_12\nSubject_12\n138\n119\n19\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_13\nSubject_13\n128\n130\n-2\n\n\n\nSubject_14\nSubject_14\n140\n122\n18\n\n\n\nSubject_15\nSubject_15\n137\n106\n31\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_16\nSubject_16\n131\n106\n25\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_17\nSubject_17\n120\n124\n-4\n\n\n\nSubject_18\nSubject_18\n128\n102\n26\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_19\nSubject_19\n139\n117\n22\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_20\nSubject_20\n135\n113\n22\nTRUE\n\n\n\n\n\n#Task 3: List practice\n\nCreate a new df similar to the one from Task 1.\n\n\n# I'm not sure what he means by \"(including the new column)\"\npre_bp_control &lt;- c(138, 135, 147, 117, 152, 134, 114, 121, 131, 130)\npost_bp_control   &lt;- c(105, 136, 123, 130, 134, 143, 135, 139, 120, 124)\ndiff_bp_control &lt;- pre_bp_control - post_bp_control\nbp_df_control &lt;- data.frame(pre_bp_control, post_bp_control, diff_bp_control)\n\n\nCreate a list with two elements (treatment (the first df), and placebo (the second df))\n\n\nmy_list &lt;- list(treatment = bp_df, placebo = bp_df_control)\nmy_list\n\n$treatment\n           patient_name pre_bp post_bp diff_bp low_bp\nSubject_1     Subject_1    130     114      16   TRUE\nSubject_2     Subject_2    128      98      30   TRUE\nSubject_3     Subject_3    116     113       3   TRUE\nSubject_4     Subject_4    124      99      25   TRUE\nSubject_5     Subject_5    133     107      26   TRUE\nSubject_6     Subject_6    134     116      18   TRUE\nSubject_7     Subject_7    118     113       5   TRUE\nSubject_8     Subject_8    126     111      15   TRUE\nSubject_9     Subject_9    114     119      -5   TRUE\nSubject_10   Subject_10    127     117      10   TRUE\nSubject_11   Subject_11    141     101      40   TRUE\nSubject_12   Subject_12    138     119      19   TRUE\nSubject_13   Subject_13    128     130      -2       \nSubject_14   Subject_14    140     122      18       \nSubject_15   Subject_15    137     106      31   TRUE\nSubject_16   Subject_16    131     106      25   TRUE\nSubject_17   Subject_17    120     124      -4       \nSubject_18   Subject_18    128     102      26   TRUE\nSubject_19   Subject_19    139     117      22   TRUE\nSubject_20   Subject_20    135     113      22   TRUE\n\n$placebo\n   pre_bp_control post_bp_control diff_bp_control\n1             138             105              33\n2             135             136              -1\n3             147             123              24\n4             117             130             -13\n5             152             134              18\n6             134             143              -9\n7             114             135             -21\n8             121             139             -18\n9             131             120              11\n10            130             124               6\n\n\n\nAccess the first list 3 different ways.\n\n\nmy_list[1]\n\n$treatment\n           patient_name pre_bp post_bp diff_bp low_bp\nSubject_1     Subject_1    130     114      16   TRUE\nSubject_2     Subject_2    128      98      30   TRUE\nSubject_3     Subject_3    116     113       3   TRUE\nSubject_4     Subject_4    124      99      25   TRUE\nSubject_5     Subject_5    133     107      26   TRUE\nSubject_6     Subject_6    134     116      18   TRUE\nSubject_7     Subject_7    118     113       5   TRUE\nSubject_8     Subject_8    126     111      15   TRUE\nSubject_9     Subject_9    114     119      -5   TRUE\nSubject_10   Subject_10    127     117      10   TRUE\nSubject_11   Subject_11    141     101      40   TRUE\nSubject_12   Subject_12    138     119      19   TRUE\nSubject_13   Subject_13    128     130      -2       \nSubject_14   Subject_14    140     122      18       \nSubject_15   Subject_15    137     106      31   TRUE\nSubject_16   Subject_16    131     106      25   TRUE\nSubject_17   Subject_17    120     124      -4       \nSubject_18   Subject_18    128     102      26   TRUE\nSubject_19   Subject_19    139     117      22   TRUE\nSubject_20   Subject_20    135     113      22   TRUE\n\nmy_list[[1]]\n\n           patient_name pre_bp post_bp diff_bp low_bp\nSubject_1     Subject_1    130     114      16   TRUE\nSubject_2     Subject_2    128      98      30   TRUE\nSubject_3     Subject_3    116     113       3   TRUE\nSubject_4     Subject_4    124      99      25   TRUE\nSubject_5     Subject_5    133     107      26   TRUE\nSubject_6     Subject_6    134     116      18   TRUE\nSubject_7     Subject_7    118     113       5   TRUE\nSubject_8     Subject_8    126     111      15   TRUE\nSubject_9     Subject_9    114     119      -5   TRUE\nSubject_10   Subject_10    127     117      10   TRUE\nSubject_11   Subject_11    141     101      40   TRUE\nSubject_12   Subject_12    138     119      19   TRUE\nSubject_13   Subject_13    128     130      -2       \nSubject_14   Subject_14    140     122      18       \nSubject_15   Subject_15    137     106      31   TRUE\nSubject_16   Subject_16    131     106      25   TRUE\nSubject_17   Subject_17    120     124      -4       \nSubject_18   Subject_18    128     102      26   TRUE\nSubject_19   Subject_19    139     117      22   TRUE\nSubject_20   Subject_20    135     113      22   TRUE\n\nmy_list$treatment\n\n           patient_name pre_bp post_bp diff_bp low_bp\nSubject_1     Subject_1    130     114      16   TRUE\nSubject_2     Subject_2    128      98      30   TRUE\nSubject_3     Subject_3    116     113       3   TRUE\nSubject_4     Subject_4    124      99      25   TRUE\nSubject_5     Subject_5    133     107      26   TRUE\nSubject_6     Subject_6    134     116      18   TRUE\nSubject_7     Subject_7    118     113       5   TRUE\nSubject_8     Subject_8    126     111      15   TRUE\nSubject_9     Subject_9    114     119      -5   TRUE\nSubject_10   Subject_10    127     117      10   TRUE\nSubject_11   Subject_11    141     101      40   TRUE\nSubject_12   Subject_12    138     119      19   TRUE\nSubject_13   Subject_13    128     130      -2       \nSubject_14   Subject_14    140     122      18       \nSubject_15   Subject_15    137     106      31   TRUE\nSubject_16   Subject_16    131     106      25   TRUE\nSubject_17   Subject_17    120     124      -4       \nSubject_18   Subject_18    128     102      26   TRUE\nSubject_19   Subject_19    139     117      22   TRUE\nSubject_20   Subject_20    135     113      22   TRUE\n\n\n\nCall the Placebo’s pre-treatment BP in a single function.\n\n\nmy_list$placebo$pre_bp_control\n\n [1] 138 135 147 117 152 134 114 121 131 130\n\n\n#Task 4: Control Flow Practice\n\nCreate a variable called “status” in each of the two data frames.\n\n\nmy_list$treatment$status &lt;- character(20)\nmy_list$placebo$status   &lt;- character(10)\n\n\nCreate categories for BP in the status variable, for the treatment data frame.\n\n\n        for(i in 1:20){\n          if (my_list$treatment$post_bp[i] &gt; 130) {\n          my_list$treatment$status[i] = \"high\"\n          #starting at 130+ and then working my way down because higher numbers won't see the 2nd and 3rd else statements.\n        } else if (my_list$treatment$post_bp[i] &gt; 120) {\n          my_list$treatment$status[i] = \"borderline\"\n        } else {\n          my_list$treatment$status[i] = \"optimal\"\n        }\n        }\n\n\nRepeat for the placebo data frame.\n\n\n        for(i in 1:10){\n          if (my_list$placebo$post_bp[i] &gt; 130) {\n          my_list$placebo$status[i] = \"high\"\n          #starting at 130+ and then working my way down because higher numbers won't see the 2nd and 3rd else statements.\n        } else if (my_list$placebo$post_bp[i] &gt; 120) {\n          my_list$placebo$status[i] = \"borderline\"\n        } else {\n          my_list$placebo$status[i] = \"optimal\"\n        }\n        }\nmy_list$placebo\n\n   pre_bp_control post_bp_control diff_bp_control     status\n1             138             105              33    optimal\n2             135             136              -1       high\n3             147             123              24 borderline\n4             117             130             -13 borderline\n5             152             134              18       high\n6             134             143              -9       high\n7             114             135             -21       high\n8             121             139             -18       high\n9             131             120              11    optimal\n10            130             124               6 borderline"
  },
