    "objectID": "HW2_A.html#task-3-list-practice",
    "href": "HW2_A.html#task-3-list-practice",
    "title": "Homework 2 - Member A",
    "section": "Task 3: List Practice",
    "text": "Task 3: List Practice\n\n1) Create a new data frame with placebo experiment\nThe code chunk that follows has most of the steps as in Task 1 and Task 2 above for placebo experiment.\n\n#From Task 1\n# 1) create vector with pre measurements using combine function\npre_bp_plc &lt;- c(138, 135, 147, 117, 152, 134, 114, 121, 131, 130)\n\n# 1) create vector with post measurements using combine function\npost_bp_plc &lt;- c(105, 136, 123, 130, 134, 143, 135, 139, 120, 124)\n\n# 2) create names for the 10 subjects using a character vector\nnames(pre_bp_plc) &lt;- paste(\"Subject\", 1:10, sep = \"_\")\nnames(post_bp_plc) &lt;- paste(\"Subject\", 1:10, sep = \"_\")\n\npre_bp_plc\n\n Subject_1  Subject_2  Subject_3  Subject_4  Subject_5  Subject_6  Subject_7 \n       138        135        147        117        152        134        114 \n Subject_8  Subject_9 Subject_10 \n       121        131        130 \n\npost_bp_plc\n\n Subject_1  Subject_2  Subject_3  Subject_4  Subject_5  Subject_6  Subject_7 \n       105        136        123        130        134        143        135 \n Subject_8  Subject_9 Subject_10 \n       139        120        124 \n\n# 3) subtract the post treatment level from pre treatment level for each subject and store as vector\ndiff_bp_plc &lt;- (pre_bp_plc - post_bp_plc)\ndiff_bp_plc\n\n Subject_1  Subject_2  Subject_3  Subject_4  Subject_5  Subject_6  Subject_7 \n        33         -1         24        -13         18         -9        -21 \n Subject_8  Subject_9 Subject_10 \n       -18         11          6 \n\n#From Task 2\n# 1) create a separate character vector for the subject names\npatient_plc &lt;- names(pre_bp_plc)\n\n# 1) create data frame using `data.frame()` function and use same column names as\n# in treatment data frame\nbp_df_plc &lt;- data.frame(\n  patient = patient_plc, \n  pre_bp = pre_bp_plc, \n  post_bp = post_bp_plc, \n  diff_bp = diff_bp_plc\n)\n\nbp_df_plc\n\n              patient pre_bp post_bp diff_bp\nSubject_1   Subject_1    138     105      33\nSubject_2   Subject_2    135     136      -1\nSubject_3   Subject_3    147     123      24\nSubject_4   Subject_4    117     130     -13\nSubject_5   Subject_5    152     134      18\nSubject_6   Subject_6    134     143      -9\nSubject_7   Subject_7    114     135     -21\nSubject_8   Subject_8    121     139     -18\nSubject_9   Subject_9    131     120      11\nSubject_10 Subject_10    130     124       6\n\n# 3) create a new column with the logical vector\nbp_df_plc$less_120 &lt;- bp_df_plc$post_bp &lt; 120\n\n# 4) print new data frame in document\nknitr::kable(bp_df_plc)\n\n\n\n\n\npatient\npre_bp\npost_bp\ndiff_bp\nless_120\n\n\n\n\nSubject_1\nSubject_1\n138\n105\n33\nTRUE\n\n\nSubject_2\nSubject_2\n135\n136\n-1\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_3\nSubject_3\n147\n123\n24\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_4\nSubject_4\n117\n130\n-13\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_5\nSubject_5\n152\n134\n18\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_6\nSubject_6\n134\n143\n-9\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_7\nSubject_7\n114\n135\n-21\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_8\nSubject_8\n121\n139\n-18\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_9\nSubject_9\n131\n120\n11\nFALSE\n\n\nSubject_10\nSubject_10\n130\n124\n6\nFALSE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n2) Create and store a list with two elements\nIt is worth noting a key difference between a vector and a list: A vector contains individual values of the same basic type, whereas a list can contain entire R objects as its elements, and those objects may or may not be the same type.\n\n#use the `list()` function to create a list and rename elements\nbp_list &lt;- list(treatment = bp_df, placebo = bp_df_plc)\n\n#inspect structure of list_bp\nstr(bp_list)\n\nList of 2\n $ treatment:'data.frame':  20 obs. of  5 variables:\n  ..$ patient : chr [1:20] \"Subject_1\" \"Subject_2\" \"Subject_3\" \"Subject_4\" ...\n  ..$ pre_bp  : num [1:20] 130 128 116 124 133 134 118 126 114 127 ...\n  ..$ post_bp : num [1:20] 114 98 113 99 107 116 113 111 119 117 ...\n  ..$ diff_bp : num [1:20] 16 30 3 25 26 18 5 15 -5 10 ...\n  ..$ less_120: logi [1:20] TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE ...\n $ placebo  :'data.frame':  10 obs. of  5 variables:\n  ..$ patient : chr [1:10] \"Subject_1\" \"Subject_2\" \"Subject_3\" \"Subject_4\" ...\n  ..$ pre_bp  : num [1:10] 138 135 147 117 152 134 114 121 131 130\n  ..$ post_bp : num [1:10] 105 136 123 130 134 143 135 139 120 124\n  ..$ diff_bp : num [1:10] 33 -1 24 -13 18 -9 -21 -18 11 6\n  ..$ less_120: logi [1:10] TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE ...\n\n\n\n\n3) Access the first list element using three different types of syntax\nWe covered three methods to access list elements.\n\n#single square brackets syntax\nbp_list[1] # returns a list containing the first element\n\n$treatment\n              patient pre_bp post_bp diff_bp less_120\nSubject_1   Subject_1    130     114      16     TRUE\nSubject_2   Subject_2    128      98      30     TRUE\nSubject_3   Subject_3    116     113       3     TRUE\nSubject_4   Subject_4    124      99      25     TRUE\nSubject_5   Subject_5    133     107      26     TRUE\nSubject_6   Subject_6    134     116      18     TRUE\nSubject_7   Subject_7    118     113       5     TRUE\nSubject_8   Subject_8    126     111      15     TRUE\nSubject_9   Subject_9    114     119      -5     TRUE\nSubject_10 Subject_10    127     117      10     TRUE\nSubject_11 Subject_11    141     101      40     TRUE\nSubject_12 Subject_12    138     119      19     TRUE\nSubject_13 Subject_13    128     130      -2    FALSE\nSubject_14 Subject_14    140     122      18    FALSE\nSubject_15 Subject_15    137     106      31     TRUE\nSubject_16 Subject_16    131     106      25     TRUE\nSubject_17 Subject_17    120     124      -4    FALSE\nSubject_18 Subject_18    128     102      26     TRUE\nSubject_19 Subject_19    139     117      22     TRUE\nSubject_20 Subject_20    135     113      22     TRUE\n\n#double square brackets syntax \nbp_list[[1]] # returns the first element itself\n\n              patient pre_bp post_bp diff_bp less_120\nSubject_1   Subject_1    130     114      16     TRUE\nSubject_2   Subject_2    128      98      30     TRUE\nSubject_3   Subject_3    116     113       3     TRUE\nSubject_4   Subject_4    124      99      25     TRUE\nSubject_5   Subject_5    133     107      26     TRUE\nSubject_6   Subject_6    134     116      18     TRUE\nSubject_7   Subject_7    118     113       5     TRUE\nSubject_8   Subject_8    126     111      15     TRUE\nSubject_9   Subject_9    114     119      -5     TRUE\nSubject_10 Subject_10    127     117      10     TRUE\nSubject_11 Subject_11    141     101      40     TRUE\nSubject_12 Subject_12    138     119      19     TRUE\nSubject_13 Subject_13    128     130      -2    FALSE\nSubject_14 Subject_14    140     122      18    FALSE\nSubject_15 Subject_15    137     106      31     TRUE\nSubject_16 Subject_16    131     106      25     TRUE\nSubject_17 Subject_17    120     124      -4    FALSE\nSubject_18 Subject_18    128     102      26     TRUE\nSubject_19 Subject_19    139     117      22     TRUE\nSubject_20 Subject_20    135     113      22     TRUE\n\n#using the $ operator syntax\nbp_list$treatment\n\n              patient pre_bp post_bp diff_bp less_120\nSubject_1   Subject_1    130     114      16     TRUE\nSubject_2   Subject_2    128      98      30     TRUE\nSubject_3   Subject_3    116     113       3     TRUE\nSubject_4   Subject_4    124      99      25     TRUE\nSubject_5   Subject_5    133     107      26     TRUE\nSubject_6   Subject_6    134     116      18     TRUE\nSubject_7   Subject_7    118     113       5     TRUE\nSubject_8   Subject_8    126     111      15     TRUE\nSubject_9   Subject_9    114     119      -5     TRUE\nSubject_10 Subject_10    127     117      10     TRUE\nSubject_11 Subject_11    141     101      40     TRUE\nSubject_12 Subject_12    138     119      19     TRUE\nSubject_13 Subject_13    128     130      -2    FALSE\nSubject_14 Subject_14    140     122      18    FALSE\nSubject_15 Subject_15    137     106      31     TRUE\nSubject_16 Subject_16    131     106      25     TRUE\nSubject_17 Subject_17    120     124      -4    FALSE\nSubject_18 Subject_18    128     102      26     TRUE\nSubject_19 Subject_19    139     117      22     TRUE\nSubject_20 Subject_20    135     113      22     TRUE\n\n\n\n\n4) Access the placebo data frame, pre_bp column\nWe can use the $ operator syntax in chain form to access a specific column in a given list and/or data frame.\n\n#Using a single line of code to access the pre_bp column in the `placebo` data frame\nbp_list$placebo$pre_bp\n\n [1] 138 135 147 117 152 134 114 121 131 130"
